---
description: TypeScript conventions for package sources
globs: packages/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

- Import inside a package through `@Collection/*` / `@Http/*`, not long relative paths.
- One class per file, default export, file named after the class.
- JSDoc on every class, interface and method: `@summary`, `@param`, `@returns`, no types in braces; `@example`
  on the public API (what `index.ts` exports). Full rules: root `AGENTS.md` › Code conventions.
- Never mutate the wrapped value: copy (`[...this.value]`) and return a new instance.
- ESLint limits: max 35 lines per function, max 3 params, max depth 2, no nested ternaries.
